# Drift k8s-node events: each violates the redis SBoB on a Kubernetes node and
# MUST fire the mapped drift rule. TIER-1 ATTRIBUTION (100070/100071) IS
# INERT on wazuh-manager 4.14.6: the shipped auditd decoder family preempts
# custom audit ROOT decoders, so the cgroup= children never run and
# sbob.pod_uid is never stamped (issue #42 documents this honestly). The
# cgroup= fields below stay in the corpus for forward-compat replay.
#   execve /usr/bin/curl          -> 100011 (SBoB drift: process ...)
#   open /etc/shadow             -> 100021 (SBoB drift: file open ...)
#   connect 185.220.101.4:4444   -> 100031 (SBoB drift: connect ...)
# attribution: cgroup data present (underscore form); INERT on 4.14.6 (see above).

